= Versions and backup <sec-backup>

Ezetta keeps your work without you thinking about it. In the project menu, "Versions and backup …" opens the dialog for it. Automatically, about once an hour, a *version* of the whole project is made in the background, in a hidden folder in the project. You can look at it, compare it with today's state and bring back a single sheet or the whole project. You make versions with a name ("Submission 1") yourself.

In addition the *backup* writes a zip file to a folder of your choice, onto a second disk for instance, and tidies up older ones. A backup can be unpacked as a new project, also on the start screen.

Nothing is ever deleted for good: sheets, groups and files go to the system trash. And every change is first written to a file and then renamed, so a crash does not leave half a file behind.
